      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Proper experimental design, involving the correct number of animals, should be a basic skill for any scientist working with animals. The authors describe a university-developed and freely available tutorial program and an interactive computer-assisted learning program, both of which guide students through the steps necessary for designing animal experiments and estimating optimal sample sizes."},
